/**
 * @defgroup compressor_catalog_units Compressor Catalog: Meaning, Units, and Data Quality
 * @ingroup compressor_modeling
 * @brief How to interpret compressor catalog records before using them as model inputs.
 * @details
 * A catalog record is a set of manufacturer-like reference values used to establish a performance
 * curve. It is not a measured operating point. Always check control compatibility, units, and the
 * unavailable-data sentinel before constructing a model.
 *
 * @warning A numeric value of -9999 means <em>unavailable or not applicable</em>. Do not convert,
 * interpolate, average, or otherwise treat it as engineering data.
 *
 * @heading{Engineering Identifiers}
 *
 * `compressorTypeId` maps to: 1 single-stage lubricant-injected rotary screw, 2 two-stage
 * lubricant-injected rotary screw, 3 two-stage lubricant-free rotary screw, 4 single-stage
 * reciprocating, 5 two-stage reciprocating, and 6 multiple-stage centrifugal.
 *
 * `controlTypeId` maps to: 1 inlet modulation without unloading, 2 inlet modulation with unloading,
 * 3 variable displacement with unloading, 4 load/unload, 5 multi-step unloading, 6 start/stop,
 * 7 inlet butterfly modulation with blow-off, 8 inlet butterfly modulation with unloading,
 * 9 inlet guide-vane modulation with blow-off, 10 inlet guide-vane modulation with unloading,
 * and 11 VFD. Select by engineering meaning and confirm the actual compressor controller; never
 * infer a control curve from the ID alone when the equipment record is ambiguous.
 *
 * @heading{Field Dictionary}
 * @symtable
 * @symrow{id; Sequential catalog record identifier; \unitless}
 * @symrow{compressorTypeId; Catalog compressor-family identifier; \unitless}
 * @symrow{model; Motor-size and catalog model label; \unitless}
 * @symrow{horsepower; Rated motor nameplate size; \horsepower}
 * @symrow{ratedCapacityAcfm; Rated delivered capacity; \acfm}
 * @symrow{ratedPressurePsig; Rated discharge gauge pressure; \psig}
 * @symrow{maxFullFlowPressurePsig; Maximum full-flow gauge pressure; \psig}
 * @symrow{controlTypeId; Catalog control-family identifier; \unitless}
 * @symrow{unloadPointPercent; Airflow at the unload transition; \percent}
 * @symrow{minUnloadSumpPressurePsig; Minimum unloaded sump gauge pressure; \psig}
 * @symrow{blowdownTimeSec; Blowdown duration; \second}
 * @symrow{unloadSteps; Number of discrete unloading steps; \unitless}
 * @symrow{modulatingPressureRangePsig; Modulating pressure band; \psig}
 * @symrow{fullLoadBrakeHorsepower; Full-load mechanical shaft power; \bhp}
 * @symrow{fullLoadBhpPowerKw; Deprecated compatibility name containing the same BHP value, not kW; \bhp}
 * @symrow{totalPackageInputPowerKw; Full-load electrical package input power; \kilo\watt}
 * @symrow{specificPackagePower; Package power per 100 acfm of rated capacity; \kilo\watt\per\hundredAcfm}
 * @symrow{noLoadPowerFullyModulating; No-load power as a percentage of full-load package power; \percent}
 * @symrow{noLoadPowerUnload; Unloaded power as a percentage of full-load package power; \percent}
 * @symrow{maxSurgePressurePsig; Centrifugal maximum surge pressure; \psig}
 * @symrow{maxSurgePressureFlowAcfm; Airflow at maximum surge pressure; \acfm}
 * @symrow{minStonewallPressurePsig; Centrifugal minimum stonewall pressure; \psig}
 * @symrow{minStonewallPressureFlowAcfm; Airflow at minimum stonewall pressure; \acfm}
 * @symrow{designSurgeFlowAcfm; Centrifugal design surge airflow; \acfm}
 * @symrow{designInletTemperatureF; Design inlet temperature; \degreeFahrenheit}
 * @symrow{designInletPressurePsia; Design inlet absolute pressure; \psia}
 * @symrow{fullLoadAmps; Full-load line current; \ampere}
 * @symrow{fullLoadEfficiencyPercent; Full-load motor efficiency; \percent}
 * @endsymtable
 *
 * @heading{Consistency Checks}
 * For a usable record, the following values should agree within catalog rounding:
 * @formula{catalog-bhp-check;
 *   P_{package}\approx\frac{BHP_{FL}(0.746)}{\eta_m}
 * }
 * @formula{catalog-specific-power-check;
 *   SP=\frac{100P_{package}}{Q_{rated}}
 * }
 * @symtable
 * @symrow{P_{package}; Full-load electrical package input power; \kilo\watt}
 * @symrow{BHP_{FL}; Full-load mechanical shaft power; \bhp}
 * @symrow{0.746; Brake-horsepower-to-kilowatt conversion; \kilo\watt\per\bhp}
 * @symrow{\eta_m; Full-load motor efficiency expressed from 0 to 1; \unitless}
 * @symrow{SP; Specific package power on a 100-acfm basis; \kilo\watt\per\hundredAcfm}
 * @symrow{Q_{rated}; Rated delivered capacity; \acfm}
 * @symrow{100; Scaling basis for specific package power; \unitless}
 * @endsymtable
 * where motor efficiency @math{\eta_m} is converted from percent to a 0-to-1 fraction and
 * specific package power @math{SP} is reported in kW/100 acfm.
 *
 * @subheading{Example}
 * A catalog row containing 5.3 bhp, 85 percent motor efficiency, 4.6 package kW, and 18 acfm gives
 * @math{5.3(0.746)/0.85=4.65\ \mathrm{kW}} and
 * @math{100(4.6)/18=25.6\ \mathrm{kW/100\ acfm}}. These agree with the rounded catalog entries
 * 4.6 kW and 25.9 kW/100 acfm. Its no-load values 65 and 50 mean 65 percent and 50 percent,
 * respectively; they are not fractions 65 and 50.
 */
